    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0580" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/920: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-04T16:00:00+02:00">November 4, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 4—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. As a result of yesterday’s plebiscite the Government announces an
                    overwhelming victory for the Monarchy. The opposition accounting for only 5
                    percent of the votes recorded. This vote cannot be accepted as a true indication
                    of popular feeling. Many Republicans undoubtedly abstained from voting and
                    plural voting by Monarchists appears to have been widespread, as well as
                    intimidation at the polls, non-issuance of opposition ballots and other means of
                    enforcing the Government’s will.</p>
                <p>By governmental decree the Regency under Kondylis has been continued until the
                    arrival of the King which is provisionally set for November 17th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
